# receiveMessage is a receiver of the language and its name is reserved: a program cannot bind it, as a method's
# name neither (RESERVED-NAME-BINDINGS; Codex K03-RESERVED-NAME-ANSWER-20261006-02: the profile exception this file
# asserted -- a declared method of that name taking precedence -- is gone).  The method is refused at its name;
# unit_next_message_method_ordinary is this program with an ordinary name.
fn: receiveMessage (int: x) int
return: x + 1

int: r 0
r: receiveMessage(3)
receiveMessage: 4
if: r != 4
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
